## Step 6 — Buyer Spec Audit

### Phase 1 — Top 2 RFQ Specs

Provided buyer specs: Application, Sheet Material, Area.

- **Application** (Storage/Godown, Car Garage, Workshop, Rooftop Shelter, Labor/Site Office, Utility Shelter): Routes the RFQ to sellers who specialise in the right product type. A seller who makes industrial storage sheds may not supply rooftop shelters or portable site offices. Application is the primary routing signal — it determines which sellers can respond. **Rank 1.**
- **Area** (200 sq ft, 300 sq ft, 500 sq ft, 1000 sq ft, 1500 sq ft, 2000 sq ft): Determines project scale and whether the seller has fabrication capacity. A seller handling 200 sq ft portable units may not handle 2000 sq ft industrial sheds. Area also directly drives the price quote — sellers need this to respond with any meaningful figure. **Rank 2.**

*(Sheet Material was considered for Rank 2 but Area is more fundamental — sellers need to know the scale before they can assess fit and price. Sheet Material is a preference that can be discussed post-connection.)*

